  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "On November 8, 2026, an incident occurred at the Darul Ma'arif Mosque in Pondok Kelapa, East Jakarta, where three worshippers were attacked during dawn prayers. Reports indicate the event began with suspicious activity outside the building. Local police have since taken the suspect, identified by initials as FP, into custody. Authorities have confiscated evidence from the scene, including an axe and gasoline. Following the apprehension, police initiated a psychiatric evaluation to determine the suspect's mental state, while formal charges have been filed that could carry a sentence of up to nine years. The Ministry of Religious Affairs and the People's Consultative Assembly of Indonesia have publicly addressed the incident, emphasizing the need for a comprehensive legal investigation into the circumstances surrounding the attack. The investigation remains ongoing as authorities work to clarify the suspect's motives.",
